1
00:00:00,890 --> 00:00:03,120
We're almost at Mt. Mud Boat.

2
00:00:03,940 --> 00:00:06,420
By the way, why are we here again?

3
00:00:06,420 --> 00:00:07,950
Um...

4
00:00:07,950 --> 00:00:11,620
This place always has
a lot of UFO sightings,

5
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:15,840
and most of them seem to happen
around the same time on New Year's Eve.

6
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:20,500
And this phenomenon apparently
occurs every seven years.

7
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:23,820
The last time there was a
sighting was seven years ago.

8
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:25,490
At least, that's what this article said.

9
00:00:26,160 --> 00:00:29,030
Well, all this information
is rather convenient.

10
00:00:32,620 --> 00:00:35,830
You've got this, Mob. We're almost there,
so don't go puking on me.

11
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:39,540
This road sure is something.

12
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:42,440
There's supposed to be a
hiking trail somewhere.

13
00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:43,310
Huh?

14
00:00:43,310 --> 00:00:44,460
What's wrong?

15
00:00:44,460 --> 00:00:48,650
I think we passed the sign for
the hiking trail a ways back...

16
00:00:48,650 --> 00:00:51,700
Uh, why didn't you mention that earlier?

17
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:54,555
I just thought he was trying to take us
(Licensed driver with little experience: 10 years)

18
00:00:54,557 --> 00:00:56,290
as far as he could with the car.
(Licensed driver with little experience: 10 years)

19
00:00:56,290 --> 00:00:57,030
Ugh!
(Licensed driver with little experience: 10 years)

20
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:02,410
We're gonna have to go in reverse until
we find enough space to make a U-turn.

21
00:01:02,940 --> 00:01:06,650
It's only 1:30 PM, so there's
probably no reason to hurry.

22
00:01:06,650 --> 00:01:10,110
Yeah, says the guy who was an hour late.

23
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:13,280
Hey, let's calm down.

24
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:15,610
The UFO's not gonna come
if we're too angry.

25
00:01:15,610 --> 00:01:16,250
Huh?

26
00:01:16,520 --> 00:01:18,490
Are you mocking me?

27
00:01:18,490 --> 00:01:21,480
And after I canceled my plans
for New Year's Eve to be here.

28
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:22,920
The hell'd you just say?

29
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:24,680
You were being all pouty,

30
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:26,983
so we were trying to be nice

31
00:01:26,985 --> 00:01:28,430
The hell's with that attitude?

32
00:01:28,430 --> 00:01:30,020
N-Now, now...

33
00:01:35,090 --> 00:01:38,220
Okay, time to put this baby in reverse.

34
00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:40,500
M-Mob!

35
00:01:47,355 --> 00:01:49,065
(MOB MOB WOW!)

36
00:01:50,185 --> 00:01:51,935
(MOB MOB WOW!)

37
00:01:53,105 --> 00:01:54,775
(MOB MOB WOW!)

38
00:01:55,945 --> 00:01:57,615
(MOB MOB WOW!)

39
00:01:59,025 --> 00:02:01,745
I realized that our youth is gray

40
00:02:01,745 --> 00:02:04,665
The origin of this uneasiness
Is yet unknown

41
00:02:04,745 --> 00:02:07,165
Trains of emotions keep running
Through my brain

42
00:02:07,165 --> 00:02:10,335
Struggling through this adolescence

43
00:02:10,455 --> 00:02:13,295
Don't disturb my deep psyche

44
00:02:13,295 --> 00:02:15,965
Who is that behind you?

45
00:02:16,085 --> 00:02:19,755
Opposing ideas creates distortion

46
00:02:19,755 --> 00:02:23,175
Exorcise all the sorrow

47
00:02:23,345 --> 00:02:26,845
So, do what you can now

48
00:02:26,935 --> 00:02:28,765
My life

49
00:02:29,015 --> 00:02:32,895
Finally, break it down

50
00:02:34,395 --> 00:02:37,235
(Want) Both greed
(Young) And honesty

51
00:02:37,235 --> 00:02:40,115
(Burn) Are growing
(1) On this chest of mine

52
00:02:40,115 --> 00:02:42,865
(Trance) I'm not waking up
(Chance) I want to wake up

53
00:02:42,865 --> 00:02:45,825
(Stance) These two different faces of mine
(1) Are standing back-to-back

54
00:02:45,825 --> 00:02:48,325
Taking things as it is

55
00:02:48,325 --> 00:02:51,745
In this free relation where
We resent each other

56
00:02:51,835 --> 00:02:54,045
Once these two become one

57
00:02:54,045 --> 00:02:56,045
That smile becomes one

58
00:02:56,045 --> 00:02:59,135
And only "1"
(MOB MOB WOW!)

59
00:02:59,795 --> 00:03:02,805
"1"
(MOB MOB WOW!)

60
00:03:03,135 --> 00:03:04,215
(MOB MOB WOW!)

61
00:03:04,215 --> 00:03:07,095
One and only "1"
(MOB MOB WOW!)

62
00:03:07,265 --> 00:03:08,805
"1"

63
00:03:08,805 --> 00:03:09,975
(MOB MOB WOW!)

64
00:03:09,975 --> 00:03:12,265
One and only "1"

65
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:18,460
(Communicating 2
~Encountering the Unknown~)

66
00:03:23,810 --> 00:03:25,430
Are you okay?

67
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:27,740
Thank goodness. There's reception.

68
00:03:28,178 --> 00:03:32,168
All right. Let's walk back
towards the hiking trail.

69
00:03:32,170 --> 00:03:35,370
I'll come back to get the car later.

70
00:03:36,660 --> 00:03:39,760
If we're going to walk, why don't we keep
going forward rather than go back?

71
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:41,290
Yeah, not happening.

72
00:03:41,290 --> 00:03:44,620
Amateurs shouldn't walk the game trails
of mountains they're not familiar with.

73
00:03:44,820 --> 00:03:47,830
I won't be able to take any responsibility
if something happens to you kids.

74
00:03:48,310 --> 00:03:52,340
Um... Sorry, I'm gonna go take a piss.

75
00:03:53,070 --> 00:03:54,920
Mob, you should go, too.

76
00:03:57,980 --> 00:03:59,690
They don't seem to be coming back.

77
00:04:00,850 --> 00:04:03,010
They aren't going number two, are they?

78
00:04:03,010 --> 00:04:05,900
Did they get lost? I'll go take a look.

79
00:04:05,900 --> 00:04:08,900
Hold it. It's dangerous to go alone.
We'll all go together.

80
00:04:09,110 --> 00:04:10,080
That way?

81
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:11,340
No, it's that way.

82
00:04:22,020 --> 00:04:24,160
Which way did we come from again?

83
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:28,300
We've definitely lost the path.

84
00:04:28,830 --> 00:04:30,700
And now there's no reception.

85
00:04:31,570 --> 00:04:34,110
Uh, we're probably gonna be
in trouble if it gets dark.

86
00:04:34,110 --> 00:04:36,410
Sh-Should we head back down?

87
00:04:36,410 --> 00:04:38,770
Whenever you get lost in the mountains...

88
00:04:38,770 --> 00:04:44,630
I've heard that it's probably safer to
head up the mountain than try to go back down.

89
00:04:45,180 --> 00:04:47,360
If we can get to a better vantage point,

90
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:49,190
we should be able to find a route.

91
00:04:49,510 --> 00:04:50,860
Oh, I see.

92
00:04:50,860 --> 00:04:54,480
I should've placed more obvious
markers along the way...

93
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:57,920
He sure seems knowledgeable,
even if he's an amateur.

94
00:04:58,700 --> 00:05:01,650
Oh, crap! I left the book back in the car.

95
00:05:01,650 --> 00:05:02,440
What? You're kidding.

96
00:05:02,700 --> 00:05:06,270
The one that has the spell for
the UFO summoning ritual?!

97
00:05:08,700 --> 00:05:10,310
It's no big deal.

98
00:05:17,720 --> 00:05:19,490
Look, it's the mountain trail.

99
00:05:19,830 --> 00:05:22,900
I think we might just make
it if we keep going!

100
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:25,470
Huh? Weren't we heading back?

101
00:05:26,810 --> 00:05:30,460
We've come this far,
so let's actually summon a UFO!

102
00:05:30,770 --> 00:05:35,010
Yeah, that's not happening. We've been
messing up left and right all day.

103
00:05:35,270 --> 00:05:37,010
Seriously, Kurata...

104
00:05:37,010 --> 00:05:41,850
Who do you think Inukawa and Saruta
painstakingly planned this all out for?

105
00:05:41,850 --> 00:05:43,970
What? Really?

106
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:47,800
Are you seriously trying to
blame this on me right now?

107
00:05:48,210 --> 00:05:53,200
I disbanded the Brainwave Club because
all of you never tried to do anything!

108
00:05:53,590 --> 00:05:55,430
Today's no different.

109
00:05:55,430 --> 00:05:57,700
I kept wondering if I should come or not!

110
00:05:58,600 --> 00:06:00,820
Because I didn't want this
very thing to happen.

111
00:06:01,330 --> 00:06:05,670
I only came because I believed you
when you said you found a telepathist.

112
00:06:06,090 --> 00:06:09,340
And yet you had the nerve to lie to me...

113
00:06:09,750 --> 00:06:15,590
None of you have any idea how I feel
getting my earnest hopes trampled on.

114
00:06:18,050 --> 00:06:19,070
How could you?!

115
00:06:19,510 --> 00:06:21,430
How could you?!

116
00:06:23,780 --> 00:06:26,770
Anyway, there's really no point
in arguing right now,

117
00:06:26,770 --> 00:06:28,510
so why don't we keep on walking?

118
00:06:28,510 --> 00:06:31,020
No, I'm going home! I'm leaving!

119
00:06:31,670 --> 00:06:34,850
I'm tired! I'm not climbing any farther!

120
00:06:35,510 --> 00:06:39,030
I'll go back alone,
so all of you can keep on going.

121
00:06:40,510 --> 00:06:41,670
Tome-san.

122
00:06:41,670 --> 00:06:43,010
Let's walk together.

123
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:53,480
Okay, fine. I just need
to keep walking, right?

124
00:06:54,860 --> 00:06:56,400
All right, let's go.

125
00:07:12,330 --> 00:07:14,720
Man, we're high up.

126
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:15,640
We did it.

127
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:18,050
4:19 PM...

128
00:07:18,050 --> 00:07:21,090
We don't have much time before
the sun's gonna set.

129
00:07:21,090 --> 00:07:27,060
Well... According to the documents,
the UFO usually appears around 5 PM,

130
00:07:27,060 --> 00:07:29,190
so let's get ready to summon it.

131
00:07:31,390 --> 00:07:35,270
Are we really doing this?
Didn't you forget the book in the car?

132
00:07:35,950 --> 00:07:39,430
Prez, you were always reading that book.

133
00:07:39,430 --> 00:07:43,790
You don't have the spell to
summon aliens memorized?

134
00:07:44,490 --> 00:07:47,190
Of course I don't.

135
00:07:47,930 --> 00:07:51,980
Isn't it enough that we all climbed
to the top of the mountain together?

136
00:07:51,980 --> 00:07:54,450
We've already made plenty
of memories today.

137
00:07:54,960 --> 00:07:56,400
This is a great view.

138
00:07:58,870 --> 00:08:00,980
What are you doing, Takenaka?

139
00:08:04,690 --> 00:08:05,740
Ahem...

140
00:08:07,940 --> 00:08:10,860
Doofa stootoo ayaabagayari...

141
00:08:11,260 --> 00:08:14,150
Prooha komo hipakaeeh...

142
00:08:16,610 --> 00:08:21,060
After creating an 8 with the rocks and
setting a foot in either circle,

143
00:08:21,060 --> 00:08:24,440
close your eyes and chant while facing
in the southwest direction...

144
00:08:24,740 --> 00:08:26,390
Hands should look like this.

145
00:08:26,860 --> 00:08:29,030
I know you remember this, Prez.

146
00:08:30,550 --> 00:08:36,470
I got pretty serious researching all of this
and before I knew it, it was morning.

147
00:08:36,470 --> 00:08:40,980
So... you weren't late because you
overslept from being too nervous?

148
00:08:41,420 --> 00:08:44,050
This is way too embarrassing to even say.

149
00:08:44,050 --> 00:08:48,660
The last thing I wanted to do was mess it
up, so I figured I'd do whatever I could.

150
00:08:48,940 --> 00:08:51,330
You were that serious about this?

151
00:08:51,670 --> 00:08:53,080
Yeah, I am.

152
00:08:53,080 --> 00:08:57,100
I decided I'd help out because these
three were so serious about all this.

153
00:08:57,540 --> 00:08:59,880
So could you believe us already?

154
00:09:01,050 --> 00:09:02,060
But...

155
00:09:02,580 --> 00:09:05,310
"Even then, I'm scared of
this going wrong.

156
00:09:06,070 --> 00:09:10,400
It's probably better to limit this
to chasing a fantasy.

157
00:09:11,400 --> 00:09:15,230
Maybe all that matters in this
is whether we had fun.

158
00:09:15,750 --> 00:09:20,650
Because my other memories with
everyone may all end up a joke, too.

159
00:09:21,420 --> 00:09:25,220
We almost got lost in the mountains
because I'm forcing my delusions on them.

160
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:30,620
I don't want to face reality
any more than this..." Apparently.

161
00:09:30,620 --> 00:09:34,910
No way! We don't think you're
forcing your delusions on us.

162
00:09:34,910 --> 00:09:37,440
This is something we wanted to do!

163
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:39,760
Before the Brainwave Club disbands.

164
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:42,570
Boys...

165
00:09:43,530 --> 00:09:44,480
Then...

166
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:46,910
Then you should've just said so earlier!

167
00:09:47,230 --> 00:09:49,110
Would it kill her to be honest?

168
00:09:49,110 --> 00:09:51,480
If that's the case, we're all doing this.

169
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:53,750
Come on, start lining up those rocks.

170
00:09:54,330 --> 00:09:57,110
Doofa stootoo ayaabagayari...

171
00:09:57,110 --> 00:09:59,790
Prooha komo hipakaeeh...

172
00:09:59,790 --> 00:10:02,580
Doofa stootoo ayaabagayari...

173
00:10:02,810 --> 00:10:03,930
Master?

174
00:10:04,580 --> 00:10:07,870
You said you researched this
all last night, right?

175
00:10:07,870 --> 00:10:10,690
Are you sure you didn't
find out anything else?

176
00:10:10,690 --> 00:10:13,500
Huh? Is your master a telepathist, too?

177
00:10:13,760 --> 00:10:16,780
No, I am not a telepathist...

178
00:10:16,780 --> 00:10:20,460
but I can read minds by observing
the subtle changes in your aura.

179
00:10:21,310 --> 00:10:23,350
Apparently, he's the kind
of guy that's a total liar

180
00:10:23,350 --> 00:10:26,090
but is good at reading people through
their actions and mannerisms.

181
00:10:26,400 --> 00:10:30,550
Well, Takenaka?
Are you hiding anything else?

182
00:10:31,750 --> 00:10:36,730
Well, the author of that occult book
was arrested two years ago for fraud.

183
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:41,690
The research in that book has no basis.

184
00:10:41,690 --> 00:10:43,680
Even this ritual is completely fake.

185
00:10:43,680 --> 00:10:45,010
Seriously?

186
00:10:45,370 --> 00:10:47,630
So you're saying this is pointless?

187
00:10:47,630 --> 00:10:48,840
What the hell?

188
00:10:49,250 --> 00:10:52,040
I-I'm sorry I didn't tell you sooner.

189
00:10:52,040 --> 00:10:56,540
I figured there was purpose in the
Brainwave Club working together, though.

190
00:10:56,830 --> 00:10:58,610
And you're exactly right.

191
00:10:58,610 --> 00:11:01,280
It's always worth it to do your best.

192
00:11:01,280 --> 00:11:04,640
All of you ended up gathering
information and took action.

193
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:06,340
That's pretty impressive.

194
00:11:06,340 --> 00:11:11,220
I'm sure this whole thing will always
be a precious memory of your youth.

195
00:11:11,510 --> 00:11:15,680
It will always remain an important
experience in your hearts.

196
00:11:16,310 --> 00:11:18,510
And you should be proud of that.

197
00:11:19,110 --> 00:11:22,590
Y-You're right. We all did our best.

198
00:11:22,590 --> 00:11:24,080
Y-Yeah.

199
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:26,080
There's no denying that we
actually did work hard.

200
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:27,120
I guess...

201
00:11:27,120 --> 00:11:30,400
All right. It's getting pretty
dark, so let's head back.

202
00:11:31,080 --> 00:11:35,460
What about the UFO sightings?
Were those also fake?

203
00:11:35,460 --> 00:11:37,910
No, apparently those really happened.

204
00:11:38,290 --> 00:11:39,450
I see.

205
00:11:46,180 --> 00:11:47,240
Then, let's do it.

206
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:49,220
We haven't tried everything yet.

207
00:11:51,840 --> 00:11:53,630
Let's send out a telepathic message.

208
00:11:53,630 --> 00:11:56,860
I'll give it my all, too,
so let's all try again.

209
00:11:57,420 --> 00:11:58,600
Mob-kun...

210
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:01,420
Prez, do you want to try it?

211
00:12:01,420 --> 00:12:02,440
Let's do it.

212
00:12:02,440 --> 00:12:03,190
Yeah.

213
00:12:03,190 --> 00:12:04,410
Come on, President Kurata.

214
00:12:04,920 --> 00:12:07,860
Boys... Thank you.

215
00:12:35,830 --> 00:12:37,480
Don't try moving too much.

216
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:39,790
Did you try too hard?

217
00:12:40,280 --> 00:12:43,460
I-I'll be okay. But...

218
00:12:44,080 --> 00:12:46,310
Dang it... I guess it didn't work.

219
00:12:53,250 --> 00:12:56,330
Why all the long faces?

220
00:12:56,330 --> 00:12:57,960
I-I mean...

221
00:12:58,220 --> 00:13:02,090
Psychics and telepathists actually exist.

222
00:13:02,660 --> 00:13:05,860
I'm sure we'll be able to
communicate with aliens someday!

223
00:13:06,420 --> 00:13:11,090
Just look at
how many stars are in the sky!

224
00:13:11,930 --> 00:13:13,480
There's no reason to hurry.

225
00:13:13,970 --> 00:13:17,260
I'm having plenty of fun being
with all of you, so it's fine.

226
00:13:20,040 --> 00:13:20,730
Huh?

227
00:13:29,030 --> 00:13:30,990
(Line up the rocks and
Doofa stootoo ayaabagayari!!)

228
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:34,500
(An Unidentified Flying Object
Actually Existed!)

229
00:13:35,350 --> 00:13:36,960
Is this for real?

230
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:38,390
It actually came?

231
00:13:38,770 --> 00:13:42,500
Wai...Wh-Wh-What do we do?!
What am I supposed to do?!

232
00:13:42,500 --> 00:13:46,200
Y-You're the one who wanted
to meet the aliens, Prez!

233
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:48,010
Y-Y-Yeah, b-but...

234
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:50,540
- Prez! Behind you! Behind you!

235
00:13:50,540 --> 00:13:52,350
- S-Something's coming!
- Prez! Behind you! Behind you!

236
00:13:52,350 --> 00:13:53,840
That was quick!

237
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:57,420
Uh, I... D-D-Do we have anything?!
Like a bug-catching net?

238
00:13:57,420 --> 00:13:59,330
Why are you thinking about
capturing them?!

239
00:13:59,330 --> 00:14:01,890
Who knows what'll happen
if we make them mad?!

240
00:14:07,610 --> 00:14:11,080
Th-This is what aliens look like?

241
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:13,040
Thin limbs...

242
00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:16,790
Giant, developed heads...
Super-smooth skin...

243
00:14:17,370 --> 00:14:20,210
Humongous, sparkly eyes...

244
00:14:20,210 --> 00:14:23,170
There's no doubt about it.
They're the real deal!

245
00:14:23,740 --> 00:14:27,140
They really do seem otherworldly...

246
00:14:27,140 --> 00:14:29,160
I wonder if we can communicate with them.

247
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:31,420
They have really pretty eyes, though.

248
00:14:32,410 --> 00:14:34,200
I don't sense any malice.

249
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:36,410
It seems like they want to shake hands...

250
00:14:36,410 --> 00:14:37,910
Wait, with me?

251
00:14:37,910 --> 00:14:39,850
I-I'd be honored!

252
00:14:39,850 --> 00:14:42,850
I can't believe I get to greet them on
behalf of Earth before anyone else!

253
00:14:43,160 --> 00:14:44,440
Hey, I really wouldn't!

254
00:14:44,440 --> 00:14:47,040
You never know what kind of
germs they're carrying.

255
00:14:47,500 --> 00:14:48,650
Master...

256
00:14:57,530 --> 00:15:00,040
Good for you, President Kurata.

257
00:15:07,050 --> 00:15:09,990
Apparently, they want to show us
the inside of their spacecraft.

258
00:15:09,990 --> 00:15:10,950
Really?!

259
00:15:10,950 --> 00:15:12,830
Sweet! That's awesome!

260
00:15:12,830 --> 00:15:14,380
Let's go, everyone!

261
00:15:16,970 --> 00:15:19,730
A-Are you sure it's okay to get on?

262
00:15:20,620 --> 00:15:22,010
I'll go, too.

263
00:15:25,610 --> 00:15:28,490
In for a penny, in for a pound, I guess...

264
00:15:51,530 --> 00:15:54,200
This really reminds me of our club room.

265
00:15:58,910 --> 00:16:01,980
They're, like, super friendly.

266
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:05,520
I sorta figured they'd be kinda scary.

267
00:16:06,920 --> 00:16:11,340
Prez, it's always been your dream to
interact with extraterrestrial lifeforms, right?

268
00:16:11,340 --> 00:16:14,730
This is your chance to ask them all kinds of
things with Takenaka as your interpreter!

269
00:16:15,040 --> 00:16:17,510
Yeah, I think I can make it work.

270
00:16:18,830 --> 00:16:24,040
R-Right... Um... Uh...

271
00:16:31,340 --> 00:16:33,100
I can't think of anything.

272
00:16:34,370 --> 00:16:37,550
Oh, I know.
Why don't we play some games?

273
00:16:37,550 --> 00:16:39,810
I always have this thing on me.

274
00:16:42,890 --> 00:16:46,150
Nice! Let's show them how it works!

275
00:17:22,570 --> 00:17:24,690
It's a new year...

276
00:17:25,760 --> 00:17:29,950
All this is going on, yet all I can think
about is the turn of the year

277
00:17:29,950 --> 00:17:32,650
and the late fees for the rental car...

278
00:17:33,590 --> 00:17:35,780
They're blinding...

279
00:17:39,200 --> 00:17:42,830
Whoa, it's almost morning.
We should head home soon.

280
00:17:43,450 --> 00:17:44,730
You're right.

281
00:17:44,730 --> 00:17:48,640
I, at least, told my parents I was spending
the night at a friend's house, but...

282
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:51,800
I mean, I guess we're all
friends now anyway.

283
00:17:54,750 --> 00:17:57,730
All right, let's start wrapping things up.

284
00:18:05,450 --> 00:18:07,290
I wonder if it's a gift.

285
00:18:07,770 --> 00:18:09,150
It's so pretty.

286
00:18:10,250 --> 00:18:13,350
It's a token of their friendship,
apparently.

287
00:18:17,100 --> 00:18:18,760
They just keep staring.

288
00:18:18,760 --> 00:18:21,540
Maybe we should give them
something in return?

289
00:18:22,090 --> 00:18:25,660
Then, I'll give them my scarf.

290
00:18:28,850 --> 00:18:32,450
Um... Then I'll give them this notebook.

291
00:18:32,880 --> 00:18:35,180
Here's my watch...
It's pretty cheap, but...

292
00:18:35,380 --> 00:18:37,130
You can have my gum.

293
00:18:37,130 --> 00:18:39,100
Here's this gaming console from Earth.

294
00:18:39,420 --> 00:18:42,140
Hm... I don't have anything.

295
00:18:42,570 --> 00:18:45,810
Maybe I can show them some of my powers.

296
00:18:47,680 --> 00:18:49,630
They seem pretty happy with that.

297
00:18:49,630 --> 00:18:51,590
Oh, that's good.

298
00:18:54,060 --> 00:18:56,730
Uh... Why are you stripping, Reigen-san?

299
00:18:57,090 --> 00:19:00,630
I was in a hurry this morning, so I'm
still wearing my pajamas underneath.

300
00:19:02,290 --> 00:19:03,380
You can have this.

301
00:19:04,100 --> 00:19:05,460
They're very happy.

302
00:19:05,460 --> 00:19:06,910
I guess anything goes.

303
00:19:14,230 --> 00:19:16,350
Thank you so much for coming to see us.

304
00:19:21,570 --> 00:19:25,760
Well, we'll be on our way now.
Let's meet again someday!

305
00:19:40,580 --> 00:19:42,520
Hey, the first sunrise of the year.

306
00:19:44,120 --> 00:19:47,100
I'll never forget today.

307
00:19:47,580 --> 00:19:51,310
I'm sure everyone else feels
the same... I just know it.

308
00:19:54,350 --> 00:19:55,540
Hey, wait.

309
00:19:56,620 --> 00:19:57,850
Where's Inukawa?

310
00:20:09,060 --> 00:20:10,540
New Year's Eve.

311
00:20:11,190 --> 00:20:13,680
I was taken away by a UFO.

312
00:20:18,580 --> 00:20:24,540
I'm going to try to convince them
to take me back to Earth.

313
00:20:25,710 --> 00:20:28,100
But I'm dealing with aliens.

314
00:20:29,420 --> 00:20:31,630
I can't communicate with them.

315
00:20:31,630 --> 00:20:34,220
This is probably going to be
a long, drawn-out battle.

316
00:20:35,260 --> 00:20:38,570
For now, I think I'm going to keep writing
down my progress in this notebook.

317
00:20:42,270 --> 00:20:48,550
The next day, they all threw me a
welcome party...? Or something.

318
00:20:48,940 --> 00:20:53,320
I had no idea what any of this stuff is,
but in the end, I chose something and ate it.

319
00:20:54,170 --> 00:20:57,060
After that,
my memories are a little foggy,

320
00:20:57,060 --> 00:21:01,560
but I think something insane happened.

321
00:21:07,150 --> 00:21:13,090
When I came to, I was in another unfamiliar
place, and my head was killing me.

322
00:21:14,620 --> 00:21:20,710
That day, I realized just how much a
little bit of gaming time would mean to me.

323
00:21:21,530 --> 00:21:23,580
But, more importantly,
I wanted to go home.

324
00:21:27,630 --> 00:21:30,610
The inhabitants of this planet
have a natural enemy.

325
00:21:30,610 --> 00:21:34,800
It's a savage monster that
tries to eat all of their crops.

326
00:21:37,640 --> 00:21:39,860
Despite being such an advanced race,

327
00:21:39,860 --> 00:21:44,210
they'd never thought of using weapons.

328
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:52,210
And so, I took care of that pest for them.

329
00:21:53,430 --> 00:21:56,590
It ended up being about the size
of the dog I have back home.

330
00:22:07,600 --> 00:22:11,800
It might be because I slew their monster,
but they treated me like a hero,

331
00:22:11,800 --> 00:22:16,940
so life on this planet
isn't so bad after all.

332
00:22:21,120 --> 00:22:25,280
I have no idea how much
time has passed now.

333
00:22:31,070 --> 00:22:32,360
Everyone!

334
00:22:33,290 --> 00:22:35,360
I have something I need to tell you!

335
00:22:41,950 --> 00:22:48,150
On the brink of loneliness, Inukawa was
able to link his thoughts with the aliens

336
00:22:48,150 --> 00:22:52,170
and tell them that he wanted
to go back home to Earth.

337
00:23:01,810 --> 00:23:06,750
If you have something you want to say,
just look them in the eyes,

338
00:23:06,750 --> 00:23:08,850
and you'll be able to get through to them.

339
00:23:09,530 --> 00:23:14,160
Inukawa realized this,
but by the time he got back to Earth,

340
00:23:14,160 --> 00:23:18,770
most of his memories had
become fuzzy and vague.

341
00:23:26,300 --> 00:23:27,240
What?

342
00:23:27,240 --> 00:23:28,220
You're joking, right?

343
00:23:28,900 --> 00:23:29,460
What?

344
00:23:29,970 --> 00:23:31,160
Really?

345
00:23:31,790 --> 00:23:33,880
Tsubomi-chan is... transferring?

346
00:23:34,790 --> 00:23:37,640
Next time on Mob Psycho 100 III Episode 9:

347
00:23:37,640 --> 00:23:37,650
Next time on Mob Psycho 100 III Episode 9:

348
00:23:37,650 --> 00:23:40,010
"Mob 1 ~Moving~"
